match.src:
comment: PH 07-Aug-2003: The original code here was this:
Ustrcpy(msgbuf, unicodeToString(((char*)responseptr) + IVAL(&responseptr->uUser.offset,0), SVAL(&responseptr->uUser.len,0)/2) );
However, if the response data is too long, unicodeToString bombs out on an assertion failure. It uses a 1024 fixed buffer. Bombing out is not a good idea. It's too messy to try to rework that function to return an error because it is called from a number of other places in the auth-spa.c module. Instead, since it is a very small function, I reproduce its code here, with a size check that causes failure if the size of msgbuf is exceeded. ****/ [1189,1884]

